CRASH-28: keep a GPV's curve at two or more points while solving

validatevalves() (CRASH-16, CRASH-06) checks at EN_openH that each GPV
has a curve with at least two points, but nothing stopped a program
from breaking that while the solver is open: EN_setcurve could replace
the curve with one point, and, once the solver reads Link.Kc (SIM-21),
EN_GPV_CURVE could assign a one-point curve. curvecoeff() then read
outside the curve's arrays on the next EN_runH. While the solver is
open, EN_setcurve now refuses fewer than two points for a GPV's curve
(error 202), and EN_GPV_CURVE refuses a one-point curve (error 211).

Requires: CRASH-06 SIM-22

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb, after CRASH-06,
SIM-22 and the patches they require:
    git apply CRASH-16_fix.patch
    git apply CRASH-06_fix.patch
    git apply SIM-19_fix.patch
    git apply SIM-21_fix.patch
    git apply SIM-17_fix.patch
    git apply SIM-22_fix.patch
    git apply CRASH-28_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index fe9992e..d9f0cf4 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -4358,6 +4358,8 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_setlinkvalue(EN_Project p, int index, int property, double valu
             if (curveIndex < 0 || curveIndex > net->Ncurves) return 206;
             // The solver uses Kc, so it must stay a valid curve while open
             if (curveIndex == 0 && hyd->OpenHflag) return 206;
+            // ... and have at least 2 points, as EN_openH requires
+            if (hyd->OpenHflag && net->Curve[curveIndex].Npts < 2) return 211;
             Link[index].Kc = curveIndex;
             Link[index].InitSetting = curveIndex;
             if (hyd->OpenHflag) hyd->LinkSetting[index] = curveIndex;
@@ -5392,6 +5394,17 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_setcurve(EN_Project p, int index, double *xValues,
     if (xValues == NULL || yValues == NULL) return 206;
     if (nPoints <= 0) return 202;
 
+    // A GPV's head loss curve needs at least 2 points. EN_openH checks
+    // this, so refuse to break it while the solver is open.
+    if (nPoints < 2 && p->hydraul.OpenHflag)
+    {
+        for (j = 1; j <= net->Nlinks; j++)
+        {
+            if (net->Link[j].Type == GPV && ROUND(net->Link[j].Kc) == index)
+                return 202;
+        }
+    }
+
     // Check that x values are increasing
     for (j = 1; j < nPoints; j++) if (xValues[j-1] >= xValues[j]) return 230;
 
